# T2 (run 1 of 2): hang shapes with the traced carry copies on c2-packed-tp4-best-strace-tpub (audits off, the timed gate twin; the lone-user sequential steps are in warmup, coding and long_real_text).
# The tpub hang risk is the two extra traces each request engine build captures after the packed captures, so both runs carry the SAME shapes: an engine build after many packed rounds
# (steady_resend), a rows=2 sequential replay (replay_concurrent4) and the four-user mixes. Runs only if T1 passed (NEEDS in ORDER.txt).
# READ: completion, every user at budget, c2_smoke_check clean, no watchdog or replay-deadline exit, the '[TPUB] carry traces engaged' line and no declined line, the four-user texts equal
# BS's on this window. A hang here is a finding against the traced publish and skips TT1-TT4. Duration (estimate): 60 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-best-strace-tpub
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady,steady_resend,replay_concurrent4,concurrent4_code_equal
